    "title": "Man sentenced in February car crash that killed Sussex County woman - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kyle Morel ,\n1 days ago A Texas man will avoid further jail time for a crash that killed a Sussex County woman earlier this year, authorities said.\nCody Bonds, 39, of Crandall, Texas, was sentenced to five years' probation and 100 hours of community service for the February crash on Route 206 in Mount Olive, the Morris County Prosecutor's Office said in a press release Sept. 15. The other driver, Jamie Lynn Aughenbaugh, 22, of Hopatcong, died from her injuries five days later.\nBonds was sentenced Sept. 11 by Superior Court Judge Ralph E. Amirata. His driver's license will also be suspended for five years, and he was credited for 17 days served in jail.\nAn investigation revealed Bonds was traveling north in the Flanders section of Mount Olive at 2:51 p.m. Feb. 3 when he crossed the double yellow center line and struck Aughenbaugh's vehicle head on, the release stated. Both drivers were injured in the crash and taken to Morristown Medical Center for treatment.\nBonds was charged in connection with the crash Feb. 24. He pled guilty in June to one count of third-degree reckless vehicular homicide and a traffic violation for failure to maintain a lane.\nThis article originally appeared on NorthJersey.com: Man sentenced in February car crash that killed Sussex County woman\n1",
